            <ArticleTitle>[Lumbalgia--how to proceed?].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>737-45</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In more than 80% of these patients no objective pathologic cause can be found and in most the disorder is self limited and benign. Nonetheless, a systematic approach to LBP should identify those patients with a serious disorder requiring special treatment. Thorough examination is the basis of treatment and management of these patients at risk for back pain disability with enormous socio-economic consequences. Psychosocial factors are at least as predictive for disability as physical.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
